#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198050 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198408 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "6b2c4733-27b9-52be-b326-b4360580b685" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Moment of a Rod About the Origin"}] :question/id #uuid "cb13bd5e-ec8a-5e5c-a45f-d710ced8c3ad" :question/math-academy-id "e-12473" :question/problem "The thin rod below has the mass density function $\\lambda (x) = (x+4)\\,\\textrm{kg/m}.$ Find the moment of the rod about the origin.\n\n![](images/7f/7f88ca365b75320795e9d38170a8586399d759696638a4bd78c73ca6c6f44b1a.png)" :question/worked-solution "The moment about the origin $O$ of a rod with mass density function $\\lambda(x)$ for $a \\leq x \\leq b$ is given by \n\n$$\nM_O = \\int_a^b x\\, \\lambda(x) \\: \\textrm{d}x.\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n\\lambda (x) = x+4, \\qquad \na=0, \\qquad \nb=3.\n$$\n\nWe calculate the moment of the rod about the origin as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{M}_{O} & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}x\\cdot (x+4)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}{x}^{2}+4x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={[\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3}+2{x}^{2}]}_{0}^{3} \\\\  & =(\\frac{{3}^{3}}{3}+2\\cdot {3}^{2})-0 \\\\  & =27.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, the required moment is $27\\,\\textrm{kg}\\cdot \\textrm{m}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198051 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198409 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "56762142-e975-5cd2-8699-3bf7a9605e93" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Center of Mass of a Rod"}] :question/id #uuid "4ebe8c87-95ba-58e2-b5d4-1bb19f231dc1" :question/math-academy-id "e-12474" :question/problem "![](images/46/461c4cb760541ea435620803689e193d13c9cb4706a59b031d37da6ffd49ab9f.png)\n\nThe thin rod above has the mass density function $\\lambda (x) = x^3.$ Given that the rod's mass is $4$ units, what is the $x$-coordinate of its center of mass?" :question/worked-solution "The center of mass of a rod placed along the $x$-axis over the interval $a \\leq x \\leq b$ whose mass density function is $\\lambda(x)$ is given by \n\n$$\n\\overline{x} = \\dfrac{M_O}{m},\n$$\n\n \n\nwhere \n\n- $\\displaystyle m = \\int_a^b \\lambda (x) \\: \\textrm{d}x$ is the mass of the rod,\n\n- $\\displaystyle M_O = \\int_a^b \\, x\\lambda (x) \\: \\textrm{d}x$ is the moment of the rod about the origin $O.$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n\\lambda (x) = x^3, \\qquad \na=0, \\qquad \nb=2.\n$$\n\nSo,  the moment of the rod about the origin is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{M}_{O} & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}x\\cdot {x}^{3}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{x}^{4}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={[\\frac{1}{5}{x}^{5}]}_{0}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}(32-0) \\\\  & =\\frac{32}{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n\\overline{x}= \\dfrac{M_O}{m} = \\dfrac{\\left(\\dfrac{32}{5}\\right)}{4} = \\dfrac{8}{5}.\n$$\n\n \n\nNote that this result makes intuitive sense. Since $\\lambda$ is an increasing function of $x,$ we would expect the center of mass to be located closer to the right endpoint and further from the left endpoint."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198052 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198410 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "70278fe3-d8dd-5f72-8bf7-f1a4a17be526" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Mass of a Thin Rod"}] :question/id #uuid "5c469b72-7ee3-5084-be63-2b7e62b42146" :question/math-academy-id "e-12475" :question/problem "The thin rod below has the mass density function $\\lambda(x) =2x\\, \\textrm{kg/m},$ where $x$ is measured in meters. What is the total mass of the rod?\n\n![](images/8c/8c8386ff979b46cd994f1ace60f681a6590856e6960e7d74c71a29bb3f0f2d1a.png)" :question/worked-solution "Given a thin rod oriented along the  $x$-axis over the interval $a \\leq x \\leq b,$ if $\\lambda(x)$ denotes the mass density function of the rod, then the total mass of the rod is given by      \n\n$$\nm = \\int_a^b \\lambda(x) \\: \\textrm{d}x.\n$$\n\nIn this case, we have\n\n$$\n\\lambda(x) = 2x, \\qquad \na=1, \\qquad \nb=3.\n$$\n\nWe calculate the mass of the rod as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m & ={\\int }_{1}^{3}2x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =[{x}^{2}]_{1}^{3} \\\\  & ={3}^{2}-{1}^{2} \\\\  & =8\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the mass of the rod is $8\\,\\textrm{kg}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198639 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198408 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "6b2c4733-27b9-52be-b326-b4360580b685" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Moment of a Rod About the Origin"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1d449c1e-1f46-5f61-9ad7-f822f5f2a1f0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot \\text{m}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186417030} {:answer/id #uuid "9a21ab4f-abbb-53fc-b207-1a91a7fd1b51" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6.8\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot \\text{m}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186417041} {:answer/id #uuid "d44b3ce5-4e08-5925-ab10-8a405b4e7b97" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6.75\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot \\text{m}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186417051} {:answer/id #uuid "e14c0f00-36c9-598c-96a2-ba74927d341f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4.75\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot \\text{m}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186417054} {:answer/id #uuid "ffcb4221-1176-5d9c-9580-81276d2bd08f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot \\text{m}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186417057}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d44b3ce5-4e08-5925-ab10-8a405b4e7b97" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6.75\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot \\text{m}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186417051} :answer-field/id #uuid "cd13b3c7-3da9-5394-8668-03f8c929a5e4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186417063}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "0d60f454-2a4f-5dfe-8bf9-970f5dda4751" :question/math-academy-id "q-162949" :question/problem "![](images/d6/d64311921135cf8dea0ec70bb0a83909fb1dba52664f4d6080de596be1693d5e.png)\n\nThe thin rod above has the mass density function $\\lambda (x)={x}^{2}+2\\,\\text{kg/m}.$ Find the moment of the rod about the origin." :question/worked-solution "The moment about the origin $O$ of a rod with mass density function $\\lambda (x)$ for $a\\le x\\le b$ is given by \n\n$$\n{M}_{O}={\\int }_{a}^{b}x\\,\\lambda (x)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n\\lambda (x)={x}^{2}+2,\\,a=1,\\,b=2.\n$$\n\nWe calculate the moment of the rod about the origin as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{M}_{O} & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}x\\cdot ({x}^{2}+2)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}{x}^{3}+2x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={[\\frac{{x}^{4}}{4}+{x}^{2}]}_{1}^{2} \\\\  & =(\\frac{{2}^{4}}{4}+{2}^{2})-(\\frac{{1}^{4}}{4}+{1}^{2}) \\\\  & =\\frac{27}{4} \\\\  & =6.75.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, the required moment is $6.75\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot \\text{m}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186417064 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198410 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "70278fe3-d8dd-5f72-8bf7-f1a4a17be526" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Mass of a Thin Rod"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1951745b-12ed-540f-b8d2-2e76d8598187" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\,\\text{kg}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186417029} {:answer/id #uuid "2b2eba11-f54c-5b8d-8056-31c66238b541" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8\\,\\text{kg}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186417031} {:answer/id #uuid "5b862d6f-8f37-5068-9257-f93374bc563f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4\\,\\text{kg}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186417035} {:answer/id #uuid "b3ef9a26-6009-519a-ae29-9fbcd3b3c4cf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3\\,\\text{kg}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186417046} {:answer/id #uuid "c1d321ac-e140-5cfc-af54-9379710575c6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6\\,\\text{kg}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186417050}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c1d321ac-e140-5cfc-af54-9379710575c6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6\\,\\text{kg}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186417050} :answer-field/id #uuid "7a609109-bbc5-5a2b-88f8-b2bbf1867c8b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186417060}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "1750e7bf-7e92-5681-92a1-454eb28ef5bc" :question/math-academy-id "q-163010" :question/problem "The mass density function $\\lambda ,$ measured in $\\text{kg/m},$ of a thin rod placed along the $x$-axis over the interval $0\\le x\\le 2$ is given by $\\lambda (x)=x+2,$ where $x$ is measured in meters. What is the total mass of the rod?" :question/worked-solution "Given a thin rod oriented along the $x$-axis over the interval $a\\le x\\le b,$ if $\\lambda (x)$ denotes the mass density function of the rod, then the total mass of the rod is given by  \n\n$$\nm={\\int }_{a}^{b}\\lambda (x)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n\\lambda (x)=x+2,\\,a=0,\\,b=2.\n$$\n\n  \n\nWe calculate the mass of the rod as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}x+2\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={[\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}+2x]}_{0}^{2} \\\\  & =(\\frac{4}{2}+2\\cdot 2)-0 \\\\  & =6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the mass of the rod is $6\\,\\text{kg}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186417066 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198410 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "70278fe3-d8dd-5f72-8bf7-f1a4a17be526" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Mass of a Thin Rod"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6834cafa-e224-515f-8cd2-a32f4c4a3f9a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6\\,\\text{kg}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186417038} {:answer/id #uuid "b19d0976-e6d7-5e98-9b30-7b81b0dfbad4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8\\,\\text{kg}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186417044} {:answer/id #uuid "bb621112-9f81-5797-a79f-6c7d609cfae5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10\\,\\text{kg}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186417047} {:answer/id #uuid "bfd2b78a-a10b-5a1b-befb-dfe0ee645ba4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "14\\,\\text{kg}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186417049} {:answer/id #uuid "f26fedd6-1d79-5b53-a483-c5459c6e306f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12\\,\\text{kg}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186417056}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f26fedd6-1d79-5b53-a483-c5459c6e306f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12\\,\\text{kg}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186417056} :answer-field/id #uuid "a83eb5c9-f2db-5800-a452-9042bb3f229a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186417061}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "66286cd3-980b-5dcd-96d4-d9a56bcaa6b2" :question/math-academy-id "q-163014" :question/problem "The mass density function $\\lambda ,$ measured in $\\text{kg/m},$ of a thin rod placed along the $x$-axis over the interval $1\\le x\\le 2$ is given by $\\lambda (x)=4{x}^{3}-3,$ where $x$ is measured in meters. What is the total mass of the rod?" :question/worked-solution "Given a thin rod oriented along the $x$-axis over the interval $a\\le x\\le b,$ if $\\lambda (x)$ denotes the mass density function of the rod, then the total mass of the rod is given by  \n\n$$\nm={\\int }_{a}^{b}\\lambda (x)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n\\lambda (x)=4{x}^{3}-3,\\,a=1,\\,b=2.\n$$\n\n  \n\nWe calculate the mass of the rod as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}4{x}^{3}-3\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =[{x}^{4}-3x]_{1}^{2} \\\\  & =(16-6)-(1-3) \\\\  & =12\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the mass of the rod is $12\\,\\text{kg}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186417068 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198409 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "56762142-e975-5cd2-8699-3bf7a9605e93" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Center of Mass of a Rod"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "13212333-e1f8-56ff-a8c7-3198d8cdf406" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{49}{20}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186417028} {:answer/id #uuid "52814006-a528-5e8d-b83f-56a2cb50f1ce" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{25}{16}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186417034} {:answer/id #uuid "85946e32-9875-5ae9-b212-a1791298f603" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{62}{15}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186417040} {:answer/id #uuid "a7a0bf2c-4e79-5ebe-80ea-3bd71ad1bd01" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{31}{12}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186417042} {:answer/id #uuid "b252df5d-3385-541f-8009-fb9c2955cb06" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{29}{18}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186417045}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "85946e32-9875-5ae9-b212-a1791298f603" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{62}{15}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186417040} :answer-field/id #uuid "1acb675f-5ff9-554d-a90a-36c18f959baf" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186417058}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "86915a7f-cf68-50dc-aafb-5f62c6d2e7e3" :question/math-academy-id "q-163020" :question/problem "![](images/ad/ad5a7d1121f6ae5a471f78477a8857b75c6a5a2008e769b1b9115c2ac880d5b6.png)\n\nThe thin rod above has the mass density function $\\lambda (x)=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt[3]{x}}.$ Given that the mass of the rod is $\\frac{9}{2}$ units, what is the $x$-coordinate of its center of mass?" :question/worked-solution "The center of mass of a rod placed along the $x$-axis over the interval $a\\le x\\le b$ whose mass density function is $\\lambda (x)$ is given by \n\n$$\n\\overset{―}{x}=\\frac{{M}_{O}}{m},\n$$\n\n \n\nwhere \n\n- $m={\\int }_{a}^{b}\\lambda (x)\\,\\text{d}x$ is the mass of the rod,\n\n- ${M}_{O}={\\int }_{a}^{b}\\,x\\lambda (x)\\,\\text{d}x$ is the moment of the rod about the origin $O.$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n\\lambda (x)=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt[3]{x}},\\,a=1,\\,b=8.\n$$\n\nSo,  the moment of the rod about the origin is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{M}_{O} & ={\\int }_{1}^{8}x\\cdot \\frac{1}{\\sqrt[3]{x}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{8}{x}^{2/3}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={[\\frac{3}{5}{x}^{5/3}]}_{1}^{8} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{5}(32-1) \\\\  & =\\frac{93}{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n\\overset{―}{x}=\\frac{{M}_{O}}{m}=\\frac{(\\frac{93}{5})}{(\\frac{9}{2})}=\\frac{62}{15}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186417067 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198409 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "56762142-e975-5cd2-8699-3bf7a9605e93" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Center of Mass of a Rod"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4a2af5bd-c1ed-59d9-a566-4a0c218db269" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{9}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186417032} {:answer/id #uuid "60ed81d6-0a1b-546f-9241-8d1dbe590600" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186417037} {:answer/id #uuid "ac9b88b6-65b8-5f2b-b100-faa9a5a6d1a6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186417043} {:answer/id #uuid "d7875743-53eb-5b08-8c40-19648e5ae5e6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186417052} {:answer/id #uuid "da5a0437-0721-5097-9076-84f467dcd2f6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186417053}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "da5a0437-0721-5097-9076-84f467dcd2f6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186417053} :answer-field/id #uuid "66d54e84-a316-51a7-bfbb-7e33fe6a2ed2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186417059}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "70f7151e-4f69-5e76-9c39-e06e4443c9a7" :question/math-academy-id "q-163029" :question/problem "Consider a thin rod along the $x$-axis over the interval $0\\le x\\le 1$ whose mass density function is $\\lambda (x)=6{x}^{2}+1.$ Find the $x$-coordinate of the center of mass of the rod." :question/worked-solution "The center of mass of a rod placed along the $x$-axis over the interval $a\\le x\\le b$ whose mass density function is $\\lambda (x)$ is given by \n\n$$\n\\overset{―}{x}=\\frac{{M}_{O}}{m},\n$$\n\n \n\nwhere \n\n- $m={\\int }_{a}^{b}\\lambda (x)\\,\\text{d}x$ is the mass of the rod,\n\n- ${M}_{O}={\\int }_{a}^{b}\\,x\\lambda (x)\\,\\text{d}x$ is the moment of the rod about the origin $O.$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n\\lambda (x)=6{x}^{2}+1,\\,a=0,\\,b=1.\n$$\n\nSo, the mass of the rod is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}6{x}^{2}+1\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={[2{x}^{3}+x]}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =2+1 \\\\  & =3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nand the moment of the rod about the origin is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{M}_{O} & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}x\\cdot (6{x}^{2}+1)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}6{x}^{3}+x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={[\\frac{3}{2}{x}^{4}+\\frac{1}{2}{x}^{2}]}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{2}+\\frac{1}{2} \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n\\overset{―}{x}=\\frac{{M}_{O}}{m}=\\frac{2}{3}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186417065 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198408 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "6b2c4733-27b9-52be-b326-b4360580b685" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Moment of a Rod About the Origin"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4ebcc29e-8dc5-5b22-b315-99b116bd7c52" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot \\text{m}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186417033} {:answer/id #uuid "5f93a53e-5bf0-5586-a8d2-b6408a97c494" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot \\text{m}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186417036} {:answer/id #uuid "794447c6-52f5-5724-9803-b4e438995276" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot \\text{m}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186417039} {:answer/id #uuid "bc9a5b2c-67cb-5952-b3aa-930af2c44107" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot \\text{m}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186417048} {:answer/id #uuid "ef2a88f5-6bb1-5f1a-8872-83524ff4e528" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot \\text{m}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186417055}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ef2a88f5-6bb1-5f1a-8872-83524ff4e528" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot \\text{m}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186417055} :answer-field/id #uuid "b97a16d2-6774-5dbd-8c93-1bf19e34efa2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186417062}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "4c3e83a3-697e-51c3-b71e-01fe636e3df8" :question/math-academy-id "q-163040" :question/problem "A thin rod with mass density function $\\lambda (x)={x}^{2}+1,$ measured in $\\text{kg/m},$ is placed along the $x$-axis over the interval $0\\le x\\le 2,$ where $x$ is measured in meters. Find the moment of the rod about the origin." :question/worked-solution "The moment about the origin $O$ of a rod with mass density function $\\lambda (x)$ for $a\\le x\\le b$ is given by \n\n$$\n{M}_{O}={\\int }_{a}^{b}x\\,\\lambda (x)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n\\lambda (x)={x}^{2}+1,\\,a=0,\\,b=2.\n$$\n\nWe calculate the moment of the rod about the origin as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{M}_{O} & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}x\\cdot ({x}^{2}+1)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{x}^{3}+x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={[\\frac{{x}^{4}}{4}+\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}]}_{0}^{2} \\\\  & =(\\frac{{2}^{4}}{4}+\\frac{{2}^{2}}{2})-0 \\\\  & =6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, the required moment is $6\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot \\text{m}.$"}]}
